Naming convention for eROSITA calibration files: 
================================================

Change log:

2010-06-02 version numbering changed from '-<nn>' to 'v<nn>' to prevent 
           potential problems with minus signs in file names (particular in 
           EXSAS) -HB


<intrume>_<name>[_<detnam>][_<filter>]_<startvalidity>v<nn>.fits


instrume: content of INSTRUME keyword in cal file
          dummy calibration for testing, etc.: sim0, sim1, ...
          eROSITA flight telescopes/cameras: whatever1...whatever7 
          calibration files applying to all telescopes/cameras: gen[eral]
          something applying to ground testing?
       
name:     type of calibration file from CCLS0001 keyword of cal file but 
          omitting the "_"; should comply with established OGIP standards 
          where possible

detnam, filter: if needed to destinguish between calibration datasets,
          these optional keywords may be used, in which case they 
          also need be part of the filename (should only be used
          where needed, e.g., to destinguish between several different 
          filters used in one camera, or between different cameras used 
          with the same mirror module, etc.).
      
startvalidity: validity start date from CVSD0001 keyword in the form 'yymmdd'

nn:       version number